LOCATION:Robinson Center
DESCRIPTION:Wed. Dec. 9 · 9:00 PM–9:30 PM · Robinson Center\nMANDATOR
 Y — production week. BA: Call Time is the time dancers should be check
 -in and backstage - Arrive 15 minutes before Call Time.\nIn Performance 
 Costumes\, Hair and Makeup.\nAll Casts are called unless a cast is named
 . SUBJECT TO CHANGE — the BA master schedule\, the weekly BA emails an
 d the BA portal are the official source. Master: https://docs.google.com
 /spreadsheets/d/1xWFCPfY5m0aK9d5dnxvALNre-6-N7Cl0kkw24rvm6cE/\n\nCOSTUME
  / HAIR / MAKEUP for Candy Cane: Russian Candy Cane — Costume (you pro
 vide): Pink Seamless Tights\, Flesh-tone camisole leotard\; Shoes: Pink 
 Ballet Shoes *Dancers of Color may wear flesh-tone ballet shoes\; Makeup
 : Full Stage Makeup - Mascara Only OK\; Hair: High Bun\, No Part\; Prop 
 (BA provides): Hoop\nFull Stage Makeup Instruction Sheet:\n•  Apply
  foundation and powder matching skintone\n•  Light skin tone eye sh
 adow over entire eye\n•  Dark brown eye shadow over crease\n• 
  Medium brown eye shadow blended over brown\n•  Black fake eyelashe
 s (note: apply mascara to own lashes before application of fake lashes)\
 n•  Apply eyeliner after lashes dry\n•  Blush on the cheeks (b
 e sure to apply plenty so dancer doesn’t look washed out in the stage 
 lights)\n•  Brown or tan on contour cheekbones\, hairline\n•  
 Use a brow pencil (or eyeshadow) to darken the eyebrows\n•  Red or 
 Dark Red Lipstick\nDancers of Color may wear flesh tone tights and flesh
  tone ballet shoes.\nCostume Care Guidelines:\n•  Handle costume pi
 eces with care while changing to prevent damage to delicate fabrics\n•
   Promptly notify Ballet Arkansas in the event of costume damage at t
 he point of discovery\, no matter how significant\n•  Never throw c
 ostumes or accessories on the floor\, or hang costumes by their elastic 
 straps\n•  Refrain from sitting on the floor while in costume\n• 
  Do not attempt to alter\, mend\, clean\, or launder any costume or a
 ccessory\n•  Never apply stage make-up while in costume and shall t
 ake great care to refrain from smudging make-up on costume during its re
 moval\n•  Refrain from the use of spray perfume or cologne while in
  costume\n•  Never wear any garment not assigned to cast member\n
 •  Do not handle or consume food or beverage while in costume\, wit
 h the exception of water\n•  Do not remove costumes from their assi
 gned dressing rooms or from the theater\n•  Remove all bobby pins u
 sed to secure head pieces and wigs following their use\n•  Return a
 ll headpieces to their assigned bags\n•  Comply fully with any and 
 all updates to Ballet Arkansas’ wardrobe policies\n•  Do not pack
  markers\, paints\, colored drinks or anything that may damage or stain 
 costumes.
